# FuseBase MCP Server Environment Variables

# ==============================================================================
# 1. Direct Token Authentication (Recommended / Zero-Browser Mode)
# As defined in FuseBase guides:
# https://thefusebase.com/guides/table-database/connect-ai-agents-to-fusebase-dashboards-with-mcp/
# https://thefusebase.com/guides/fusebase-ai/connect-external-ai-agents-to-fusebase-with-mcp/
# Note: When tokens are configured, FUSEBASE_HOST & FUSEBASE_ORG_ID are auto-discovered via whoami.
# ==============================================================================
FUSEBASE_GATE_TOKEN=your_gate_mcp_token_here
FUSEBASE_DASHBOARDS_TOKEN=your_dashboards_mcp_token_here
# Or unified token:
# FUSEBASE_TOKEN=your_api_token_here

# ==============================================================================
# 2. Session Cookie Authentication (Interactive / Headless Playwright Mode)
# Required only if collaborating on Y.js CRDT WebSockets or using session cookies
# ==============================================================================
FUSEBASE_HOST=yourorg.nimbusweb.me
FUSEBASE_ORG_ID=your_org_id
# FUSEBASE_COOKIE=your_cookie_string_here

# ==============================================================================
# 3. Tool Tier Configuration
# "core" (default, 34 tools) or "all" (175 tools including databases, portals, CLI, automations, tokens)
# ==============================================================================
# FUSEBASE_TOOLS=all

# ==============================================================================
# 4. Live Test Suites (npm run test:live)
# Live suites create and delete data, so they only run in the workspace named here.
# ==============================================================================
# FUSEBASE_WORKSPACE_ID=your_sandbox_workspace_id
# Portal invite / magic-link tests send real email; set to an address you control to run them.
# FUSEBASE_TEST_INVITE_EMAIL=you+fusebase-tests@example.com

# ==============================================================================
# 5. HTTP Transport (MCP_TRANSPORT=http)
# Every HTTP session uses the FuseBase credentials above, so access is locked down:
# the server binds 127.0.0.1 by default and refuses a non-loopback MCP_HOST without a token.
# ==============================================================================
# MCP_TRANSPORT=http
# MCP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=3000
# MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=generate_with_openssl_rand_hex_32
# MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=my-server.local            # extra Host header names (comma-separated)
# MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173    # browser origins allowed to call the server
# FUSEBASE_DOWNLOAD_DIR=/path/for/attachments  # where download_attachment may write (default data/downloads)
# FUSEBASE_CLI_ALLOWED_DIRS=/path/to/apps       # extra directories the CLI tools may run in

# ==============================================================================
# 4. Encrypted Secret Storage
# Cookies, tokens and agent credentials saved by the auth scripts are encrypted with
# a random key kept in <data dir>/.key (created on first use, owner-only). In Docker
# or CI, set FUSEBASE_SECRET_KEY (64 hex chars or base64 of 32 bytes) instead and
# keep it out of the image. FUSEBASE_DATA_DIR moves the data directory.
# ==============================================================================
# FUSEBASE_SECRET_KEY=
# FUSEBASE_DATA_DIR=/app/data

# ==============================================================================
# 5. 1Password (recommended; see docs/1PASSWORD.md)
# Keep secrets in 1Password and put only op:// references here, then start the server
# with: op run --account <your-account>.1password.com --env-file=.env -- node dist/index.js
# ==============================================================================
# A. Vault items:
# FUSEBASE_GATE_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<gate token item>/credential
# FUSEBASE_DASHBOARDS_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<dashboards token item>/credential
# FUSEBASE_SECRET_KEY=op://<vault>/<key item>/password
#
# B. Or a 1Password Environment, read by a read-only service account:
# FUSEBASE_OP_ENVIRONMENT_ID=<environment id>
# FUSEBASE_OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<service account token item>/credential
#
# Account for resolving references without op run (one approval per start):
# FUSEBASE_OP_ACCOUNT=<your-account>.1password.com
